# =============================================================================
# .gitignore — organized into pattern rules. Sections:
#   1. Python / build / OS
#   2. Secrets & local environment
#   3. Root-level detritus & stray downloads
#   4. data/raw source exclusions (raw downloads; provenance comments verbatim)
#   5. data/clean curated tree (derived, disposable)
#   6. Dashboard / codebase-site generated data
#   7. results/ forecast & scenario caches
#   8. results/calibration slim-bundle rules (heavy regenerable intermediates)
#   9. results/calibration & results/hindcast scratch families
#  10. Misc local caches
# One-off, session-specific scratch-dir names are intentionally NOT enumerated:
# any bundle's heavy contents are already covered by the §8 slim-bundle rules,
# and the recurring scratch families are covered by §9.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Python / build / OS
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
dist/
build/
.DS_Store

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Secrets & local environment — never commit credentials. Keys resolve at
#    runtime from a local, untracked .env; commit a keys-only .env.example.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Root-level detritus & stray downloads. Extract archives into data/raw/
#    instead; scratch scripts belong in scripts/probes/, logs are transient.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
/*.zip
/*.log
/scratchpad_*.py
/probe_run*.log
/scratch/
/scratchpad/
/scratchpad_logs/
/scratch_hindcast/
/scratch_logs/
/logs/
/logs_g10/
# Local compatibility shim: symlinks (inputs/ -> data/raw/...) so tooling that
# still records the pre-W1-relocation inputs/ paths in old bundle configs can
# resolve them; never a committed artifact.
/inputs/
# Agent tool worktrees (per-session isolated worktrees, not repo content)
.claude/worktrees/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. data/raw source exclusions — raw downloads are re-fetchable and too large
#    for the push endpoint; provenance comments kept verbatim.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-ISO EIA-860 override CSVs — raw source files (parquet/json) are committed
data/raw/eia-860/*.csv

# PJM energy market offers raw monthly parquets — gitignored (large corpus +
# PJM DataMiner2 redistribution terms, see docs/data-licensing.md §4). Refetch/
# curate instructions: data/raw/pjm-energy-offers/README.md.
data/raw/pjm-energy-offers/*
!data/raw/pjm-energy-offers/README.md

# CAISO OASIS DAM public-bid daily zips (~1,096 files / 0.5-0.9 GB for
# 2023-2025): refetch with scripts/fetch_caiso_public_bids.py (see
# data/raw/caiso-public-bids/README.md).
data/raw/caiso-public-bids/*
!data/raw/caiso-public-bids/README.md

# MISO annual bc_HIST source mirrors (~20-70 MB raw each; validation layer
# only, rule 13): refetch with scripts/data/fetch_miso_bc_hist.py (see
# data/raw/transfer-constraint-binding/MISO/README.md provenance table).
data/raw/transfer-constraint-binding/MISO/*_bc_HIST.csv.gz

# PJM DataMiner2 DA virtual-bid feeds (hrl_da_incs_decs, hrl_dmd_bids): same
# non-member redistribution restriction as pjm-energy-offers; refetch with
# scripts/fetch_pjm_da_virtuals.py (see data/raw/pjm-da-virtuals/README.md).
data/raw/pjm-da-virtuals/*
!data/raw/pjm-da-virtuals/README.md

# NYISO MIS public DAM zonal LBMP monthly archives (36 zips, ~13 MB): raw
# source of nyiso_proxy_lmp_hourly_NEISO.parquet (committed). Regenerable
# byte-identical from the stable public URLs
# (http://mis.nyiso.com/public/csv/damlbmp/YYYYMM01damlbmp_zone_csv.zip) —
# too large for this remote's push limit, so gitignored like the PJM
# energy-offer corpus above; fetch + rebuild:
# scripts/build_nyiso_proxy_lmp_neiso.py (docstring has the curl loop).
data/raw/lmp-data/NYISO/*damlbmp_zone_csv.zip
data/raw/lmp-data/NYISO/*realtime_zone_csv.zip
# Transient outer container the derive_actual_lmp NYISO DA reader consumes
# (assembled locally from the monthly damlbmp zips above; same re-fetchable
# lineage — the committed actual_lmp_hourly_NYISO.parquet is the durable
# record, per the holdout-register staging precedent).
data/raw/lmp-data/NYISO/NYISO_zonal_hourly.zip

# NYISO ancillary-services raw pull cache.
data/raw/NYISO-AS/raw/
# ISO-NE hourly reserve-requirement window CSVs (75 files, 2023-2025): kept
# out of the pack per the NYISO-archive precedent; regenerate with
# scripts/fetch_neiso_reserve_requirements.py (README.md in that dir).
data/raw/NEISO-AS/requirements/requirements_*.csv
# ISO-NE DA energy-offer daily CSVs (~1.4 GB for 2023-2025): gitignored, same
# precedent; regenerate with scripts/fetch_neiso_da_energy_offers.py.
data/raw/NEISO-AS/da-energy-offers/hbdayaheadenergyoffer_*.csv

# NOAA GHCN-Daily raw per-station pull cache for scripts/fetch_zone_temperature.py
# (re-fetchable; --no-fetch re-derives the zone CSVs from it). NEVER commit — the
# raw station archives are hundreds of MB and trip the remote's 413 push limit.
data/raw/*-weather/_ghcn_cache/

# Derived binned-fleet cache (side output of the fleet loader)
data/raw/_processed-legacy/*.parquet
# The EIA-923 extracts ARE committed: they are small (~16 KB cost,
# ~225 KB generation) and produced once by
# scripts/process_f923_fuel_costs.py; the dispatch fuel resolver and
# the calibration diagnostic read them at runtime.
!data/raw/_processed-legacy/eia923_monthly_fuel_costs.parquet
!data/raw/_processed-legacy/eia923_monthly_generation.parquet
# Derived CAMPD reference artifacts — per-plant parasitic-load factors and
# emission rates, read at runtime by the dispatch LP and calibration report.
!data/raw/_processed-legacy/parasitic_load_factors.parquet
!data/raw/_processed-legacy/plant_emission_rates.parquet
# Per-year EIA-860 plant-level CHP flag lookup (~0.5 MB), produced by
# scripts/build_eia860_chp_by_year.py from the committed EIA-860 release zips.
# The fleet loader reads it so a multi-year backcast buckets each year's gas
# cogens with that year's CHP designation instead of the latest snapshot's.
!data/raw/_processed-legacy/eia860_chp_by_year.parquet
# Class-totals cache for scripts/derive_offer_curve_jacobian.py (rebuilt on
# demand from the calibration bundles; the CSV it derives IS committed)
data/raw/_processed-legacy/.offer_curve_jacobian_cache.json

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. data/clean curated tree is DERIVED and disposable: regenerated from
#    data/raw by the per-datatype scripts/curate_*.py (each writing through
#    scripts/lib/clean_io.write_clean). Sessions commit the curation script + its
#    test, never the generated parquet. The schema YAMLs and the data dictionary
#    under data/dictionary/ ARE committed (they are the contract, not output).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
/data/clean/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Dashboard / codebase-site generated data. frontend/data/backcast/*.js
#    (manifest/benchmark/completeness) ARE committed (raw-checkout preview via
#    the bc-data.js fallback); the "Deploy site to GitHub Pages" workflow is
#    their single writer on main. The codebase-site subset below is generated at
#    deploy time by scripts/build_codebase_site_backcast.py and never committed.
#    The RETIRED keeper/status monoliths (sharded per-ISO 2026-07-19 into
#    keepers/<ISO>.json + status/<ISO>.js so parallel promotions never collide)
#    are ignored so a stale tool can't resurrect them into a commit.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/codebase-site/data/backcast/
frontend/data/backcast/keepers.json
frontend/data/backcast/status.js

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 7. results/ forecast & scenario caches — transient per-ISO LP outputs keyed by
#    cache_key (results/<ISO>/<cache_key>/). Only results/calibration/ bundles
#    are tracked; capacity-expansion forecast runs are reproducible from config.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
/results/ERCOT/
/results/CAISO/
/results/PJM/
/results/MISO/
/results/NYISO/
/results/NEISO/
# Full-horizon forecast runs and ad-hoc forecast probes: disposable diagnostic
# cache, never committed (forecast probes are not dashboard-registered —
# CLAUDE.md rule 15/16; regenerate from config). Covers the run dirs and their
# loose top-level run logs (e.g. results/probe-pjm-rps.log).
/results/full-horizon/
/results/ff-t1f-baseline/
/results/probe-*/
/results/verify-*/
/results/*.log
# warm-start solver benchmark output + captured-LP cache (generated by
# scripts/bench_warmstart.py / bench_warmstart_xyear.py; measured numbers live
# in docs/cross-year-warmstart.md).
/results/warmstart_bench.txt
/results/warmstart_xyear_bench.txt
/results/warmstart_xyear_capture.pkl
# Outage-gate audit scratch.
/results/outage_gate_audit/
# Stage-0 regression goldens (docs/handoffs/orchestrator-unification-plan-2026-07.md
# §7.3): multi-GB re-solved keeper bundles used only for before/after stage
# comparison. The bundles live in <stage-tag>/<ISO>/ subdirs — ignore those (they
# trip the remote's 413 push limit); the hashes-only <stage-tag>/manifest.json
# stays tracked as the committed deliverable.
/results/regression-goldens/*/*/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 8. results/calibration slim-bundle rules. Bundles are committed slim: only the
#    text files (meta/run_config/metrics/legitimacy_diagnostics/attestation/
#    SUMMARY) + the dashboard payload. The per-hour dispatch dir, system/storage/
#    btm/scarcity/availability/posture/flows parquets, floors, solve logs and the
#    captured model_changes.diff are large regenerable intermediates. Rules cover
#    both the flat (results/calibration/<name>/) and ISO-scoped
#    (results/calibration/<ISO>/<name>/) bundle layouts.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
results/calibration/*/model_changes.diff
results/calibration/*/dispatch/
results/calibration/*/*.parquet
results/calibration/*/floors/
results/calibration/*/solve.log
results/calibration/*-capdel-probe.log
results/calibration/*/_shared/
results/calibration/_shared/
results/calibration/logs/
# ISO-scoped (two-level) bundle internals — the single-* rules above miss them.
results/calibration/*/*/dispatch/
results/calibration/*/*/floors/
results/calibration/*/*/system.parquet
results/calibration/*/*/storage.parquet
results/calibration/*/*/btm.parquet
results/calibration/*/*/availability_rcpf*.parquet
results/calibration/*/*/scarcity*.parquet
results/calibration/*/*/posture.parquet
results/calibration/*/*/flows.parquet
results/calibration/*/*/solve.log
results/calibration/*/*/_shared/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 9. results/calibration & results/hindcast scratch families — recurring
#    throwaway-probe naming (rule 14/16: never registered keepers; regenerable
#    from run_config.json). One-off per-session dir names are NOT enumerated;
#    their heavy contents are already ignored by §8.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
results/calibration/*probe*/
results/calibration/_diag_*
results/calibration/caiso_diag_*/
results/calibration/miso_diag_*
results/calibration/*_repro_A/
results/calibration/*_y20[0-9][0-9]/
# Per-year probe accumulator scaffolding (e.g. results/calibration/_miso70_acc/
# {main,base}/y2023): fully disposable intermediates — the registered final
# bundles are the deliverable.
results/calibration/_*_acc/
results/calibration/MISO/_diag_*
results/calibration/MISO/_repro_logs/
# Capacity-hindcast bundle internals are reproducible from the recorded config;
# the committed deliverable is the slim set (meta.json + score.json + frontend
# sidecar + report). Ledgers/configs committed under the earlier convention stay
# tracked (gitignore never untracks).
results/hindcast/*/*/*/year_*.parquet
results/hindcast/*/*/*/evolution_*.json
results/hindcast/*/*/*/year_*_floor_retentions.json
results/hindcast/*/*/*/config.yaml
results/hindcast/*/*/*/*.parquet
results/hindcast/*/run_config.yaml
results/hindcast/*.log
results/hindcast/*/run.log

# FF-2B base-year adequacy solves (results/ff2b-after/<iso>, run via
# run_full_horizon at T0 scale for the 2026 I7 check the *-ff-2b-adequacy
# sidecars point to): the slim deliverable is full_horizon_summary.json +
# evolution_*.json (the capacity accounting); the dispatch parquet and config
# are reproducible from the recorded run. The ff2b-before/ baselines are
# unreferenced diagnostic scratch (disposable, no sidecar points at them).
/results/ff2b-before/
results/ff2b-after/*/*/*/year_*.parquet
results/ff2b-after/*/*/*/config.yaml

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 10. Misc local caches (docs/handoffs driver scratch — the committed
#     deliverables are the driver-battery-<iso>-<date>.{md,json} memos).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/handoffs/_fom_grid_cache/
docs/handoffs/_foresight_ab_cache/
docs/handoffs/_battery_cache_*/
docs/handoffs/_battery_metrics/
